You are given a binary tree, which is a structure made up of nodes.

Each node can have:
- A value.
- A left child.
- A right child.
The question asks you to visit every node in a particular order and return their values in an array (list).

That particular order is called Inorder Traversal.

It means:
Left → Root → Right
- Left: Visit the left subtree.
- Root: Visit the current node.
- Right: Visit the right subtree.

***********
Start from the root.
Keep moving left as long as a left child exists.
Push each visited node into the stack.
When you reach null, pop a node from the stack.
Add its value to the result array.
Move to its right child.
Again, repeat the same process.

**************************************

class Solution {
    public List<Integer> inorderTraversal(TreeNode root) {

        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        Stack<TreeNode> stack = new Stack<>();

        TreeNode current = root;

        while (current != null || !stack.isEmpty()) {

            // Keep moving left
            while (current != null) {
                stack.push(current);
                current = current.left;
            }

            // Pop the node and add its value
            current = stack.pop();
            result.add(current.val);

            // Move to the right child
            current = current.right;
        }

        return result;
    }
}
